  {
    "number": 77,
    "title": "perf: prepare real early source measurements; budgets pending",
    "body": "Refs #30. Draft preparation for the early baseline/budget stage only. This is not an accepted early-stage delivery and does not release Hub #3.\n\nThe candidate measures real pinned Nanoleaf SQLite admission with worker launch excluded, and both actual released lifecycle validators in a disposable external npm consumer. It retains raw WSL samples, source/archive/tool hashes, process and clock boundaries, repeated profiles and observed load/resource data. It adds reusable negative/timeout/provenance checks and a real released-package consumer check to the existing Linux/Windows Python matrix. Existing CI jobs remain required.\n\nLocal Node 24/Python 3.14 build, type, controller-contract, lifecycle, MCP, package and workflow checks pass. Performance checks cover 14 cases plus both real validators and modified-corpus rejection. Nine admission profiles and six validator profiles completed. These are observations, not product budgets.\n\nMissing matched Windows measurements, actual hook-return/helper coverage and frozen numeric budgets block early delivery. WSL interop still fails a version-only PowerShell probe with `UtilBindVsockAnyPort:307: socket failed 1`. The active OpenSpec change `gh-30-shared-monitor-performance` remains unfinished and unarchived. No guide completion claim, merge, overall issue completion or dependent implementation is authorized by passing tooling CI.\n\nNo installed clients, personal hooks/settings, live state, device operations or evaluation runs are included. Pinned upstream Python files are measurement inputs, not Hub provider implementations. The lifecycle archive is the real released 1.0.0 package, not a checkout-relative dependency.\n\nReview corrections retain failing regressions for dependency shadowing and SQLite connection cleanup. Exact-byte Git attributes preserve pinned sources/receipts in Windows checkouts. All admission and validator profiles were rerun with their corrected tools; current candidate is `14c5f733cb48201014abea0e9043b1959e6690c6`. Both independent preparation reviews are clear; all twelve current-head PR jobs passed in run34289096133 and all twelve branch jobs passed in run34289093226. The early stage remains incomplete.\n",
    "state": "open",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/77",
